  "Notes": "All-dielectric Fabry-Perot comparison filter at 2 um (Fig. 3(b))\nSpecification: Narrow-band all-dielectric Fabry-Perot used only for comparison.\nReported: Fig. 3(b) (calculated, plot only): psi = tau0' = 1 at all wavelengths (lossless); 1/(1+F sin^2 phi) has a narrow pass band at 2.0 um, sideband rising toward 1 near 3.3-3.5 um and a sideband/dip structure near 1.0-1.3 um.\nNotes: Label glass|HLHL|HH|LHLH|glass, mu_H = 2.748, mu_L = 1.32, mu_g = 1.5. The 2-QWOT HH spacer is one layer (9 layers). Design wavelength not stated in the caption; 2.0 um assumed from the pass-band position in the plot and the paper's 2 um context. Symmetric, constant indices, normal incidence.\nLayers from Fig. 3(b) label and caption, p. 655; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
